WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:05.749 align:start position:0%
 
feeding  and milking the cows cleaning out the  stables  a daily routine for farmer byram alician  turk  but the stall next door holds his true  passion  his dromedaries they are treated to a  daily wellness program  byram massages their joints and necks  not to improve their carrying of burdens  but to prepare them  for wrestling matches  they love these massages it relaxes them  and gives them energy  the drum dribbles don't look aggressive  on first sight  but bioram knows why they wear their  muzzles  it's in their nature to assert  themselves against rivals  that's why we don't have to train them  for the matches we just give them love  a town on turkey's aegean sea coast  there's no desert here  and camels aren't indigenous but the  inhabitants forebears came from central  asia  and brought the tradition of camel  wrestling with them  a big match is scheduled this weekend in  this dusty sports arena  the first spectators have already  arrived and the atmosphere is festive  the contestants have come from far and  wide  first the animals wait in a parking  garage  then the richly adorned candidates strut  their stuff in a procession through the  town of thirty thousand  most of the owners are poor farmers who  hope to earn a little extra cash with  the prize money  for boston the camel wrestling match is  the high point of the year  camel wrestling is a centuries-old  tradition we cultivate it  and by doing that we honor our nomadic  ancestors  byram has come for a look at the  competition before the matches begin  the owners all know each other almost  all winter long the camel's rushing  season they went their way along the  aegean coast to the various arenas  some animals like to attack from the  left others from the right  i know the wrestling style of most of  the animals here  on byram's farm the animals are prepared  for the fight  they're fitted with heavy saddles the  competition is not only about a few  hundred euros in prize money  but also the glory of victory everyone's  in suspense  the dromedaries too  they know something's different today  are we going to make it to the finals  will everything come off without any  accidents  these thoughts stress both the camel and  me  then the caravan sets off it's five  kilometers to the arena  on match days the camel drivers all wear  traditional  orange and white plaid neckerchiefs  people have been streaming into the  venues since early morning  some spectators follow the route of the  camel wrestling matches from one coastal  town to the next  a lot of rocky turkish snaps is being  downed at the picnic tables  rocky and camel wrestling are both part  of the fun you need both  a stand sells camel sausage so even  camels that can't wrestle anymore  contribute to the celebration  the athletes march one last time past  the grandstand  where the local notables have their  places  the first two contestants are released a  match lasts five minutes  the winner is the camel that knocks over  his opponent pushes him aside  or gets him in a headlock there are  different weight classes and a referee  to keep his animal from being injured an  owner can give up by throwing the lead  rope into the middle  this is tunahan he foamed at his mouth  and looks quite aggressive  the owners say that the camels love to  wrestle but the criticism of animal  rights activists to this tradition  is getting louder  the people in boston pay no attention to  such criticism  byram's strongest bull camel is up next  his name is ozgoorhan and byram wants  him to make the finals  the spectators are having a grand time  ausgurhan throws himself on his  opponent's neck  but the other bull manages to stay on  his feet  byram doesn't leave his camel's side the  match ends in a draw  i'm happy nevertheless it was a fair  fight  he fought well and we were actually  ahead on points  despite the tie ozgurhan and his proud  owner receive a trophy  now they can rest from their exertions  it'll be another year before the arena  is open to the dromedaries again

